  id: PY_RUN_12_LISTS_APPEND
  language: 1
  topic: Lists
  difficulty: 0
  questionType: 2
  questionText: Fill in the line that adds the text "map" to the end of the list
    items.
  code: '____

    print(len(items))'
  answerFormat: 2
  choices: []
  correctChoiceIndex: 0
  monospaceChoices: 0
  acceptedAnswers: []
  caseSensitive: 1
  referenceFill: items.append("map")
  runTests:
  - setup: 'items = ["key", "torch"]'
    expectedOutput: 3
  - setup: 'items = []'
    expectedOutput: 1
  - setup: 'items = ["a"]'
    expectedOutput: 2
  explanation: append() adds one value to the end of a list. The list then has one
    more item, so len(items) goes up by 1.
  hint: Lists have a method that adds a value to the end. Write the list name, a
    dot, then the method.
  wrongChoiceFeedback: []
  wrongAnswerFeedback: Write list name, a dot, the method that adds to the end, then
    the value in brackets (text needs quotes).
